The message originates in **h11**, then is translated by **httpcore** and finally by **httpx**. In this deployment, “peer” is the endpoint on the other side of the tunneled stream—normally the vendor origin as observed through the proxy; the proxy can also be the component that closes the tunnel, and the parser cannot distinguish which hop generated the EOF.

